+# CRM3 App v4.2_R1 Canonical-Main Implementation Report
+
+## Governing direction
+
+v4.2_R1 remains a forward migration to the new maintenance-workflow architecture. Canonical main is used to preserve proven source, security and governance guarantees—not to retain obsolete authority paths or disposable development data.
+
+## Canonical baseline
+
+- branch: `main`
+- commit: `633c58bb0d936011e391b42627f8b8f02c510e95`
+- tree: `2f547a79e79076c70dd15ae8b85a7ad70c9fa018`
+
+The 410-path canonical source collector reconciles as 347 byte-identical, 63 successor-modified and zero missing paths.
+
+## R1 improvements
+
+1. Exact canonical-main source and Isar baselines are embedded and executable.
+2. Stage 2D-F2, programme-ledger, Android and workflow authorities remain byte-identical.
+3. PR39 websocket-driver closure remains exact in root and Functions locks.
+4. Backend user approval/roles are parsed through one generated-policy-aligned validator across six backend surfaces.
+5. Full-collection read-only integrity sweep detects documents hidden from ordered client queries.
+6. Trial runs only in a disposable workspace.
+7. Both Firebase build files are exact-hash bound to canonical main.
+8. Node, npm and Java are added to the pinned Flutter/Dart gate.
+9. Skipped/mismatched runs can report only diagnostic outcomes.
+10. Lockfiles and handwritten source are protected after dependency resolution/codegen.
+11. Authentic generated Isar output is compared against all 16 canonical collection/property/index definitions.
+12. Fresh install is distinguished from in-place upgrade.
+13. The incorrect `1083` path count is corrected to 229 file paths.
+14. Local-only `57be731…` offline-signing work is classified and deliberately not merged wholesale.
+15. Clean cutover is ratified for development-only data, subject to read-only inventory before reset.
+
+## Mutation boundary
+
+No Git repository, remote ref, Firebase backend, production data or device was changed while creating this package.
