+# v4.2_R1 Authoritative Local Laboratory Runbook
+
+## Purpose
+
+This laboratory proves the canonical-main-reconciled successor source without changing the real repository or any Firebase backend.
+
+The script:
+
+- verifies the pristine package;
+- copies it to a disposable workspace;
+- exact-hash binds the two Firebase build inputs from canonical main;
+- enforces Flutter, Dart, Node, npm and Java versions;
+- proves all lockfiles stable;
+- runs authentic Isar generation;
+- checks the post-codegen allowed delta;
+- proves all inherited Isar IDs remain exact;
+- runs source audits, Functions tests, Flutter analysis/tests and debug APK build;
+- optionally runs Rules/Functions emulator gates;
+- optionally installs only on a device where the package is absent;
+- produces a sealed evidence ZIP.
+
+It does not push, merge, tag, deploy, write production data, uninstall an app or clear device data.
+
+## Required inputs
+
+- extracted v4.2_R1 candidate;
+- clean canonical repository at `C:\Users\abhis\AndroidStudioProjects\crm3_baf_ops` containing:
+  - `lib/firebase_options.dart`;
+  - `android/app/google-services.json`;
+- pinned toolchain:
+  - Flutter `3.44.0`;
+  - Dart `3.12.0`;
+  - Node `22.15.0`;
+  - npm `10.9.2`;
+  - Java `21.0.11`.
+
+The harness exact-binds:
+
+- `firebase_options.dart`: `07912823FCC37500C785BE26741B3930087D7A47F02F5E2268F7C7FC1A6031DE`;
+- canonical-main `google-services.json`: `DBD4450D064E6FE68D2F809A8A81B1FE5AC6E96E390F8F0B1762938D0EF5FE6D`.
+
+The historical registration-source hash `730A044F...` is not substituted for the committed build file.
+
+## Recommended complete run
+
+From PowerShell 7:
+
+```powershell
+Set-Location "$HOME\Downloads"
+
+$Zip = Get-ChildItem "$HOME\Downloads" -File |
+  Where-Object Name -Like "CRM3_APP_V4_2_R1_CANONICAL_MAIN_LOCAL_LAB_CANDIDATE*.zip" |
+  Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending |
+  Select-Object -First 1
+
+if (-not $Zip) { throw "v4.2_R1 candidate ZIP not found." }
+
+$CandidateRoot = "$HOME\Downloads\CRM3_APP_V4_2_R1_CANONICAL_MAIN_LOCAL_LAB_CANDIDATE"
+Remove-Item $CandidateRoot -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
+Expand-Archive -LiteralPath $Zip.FullName -DestinationPath $CandidateRoot -Force
+
+$Candidate = Get-ChildItem $CandidateRoot -Directory |
+  Select-Object -First 1
+$Script = Get-ChildItem $Candidate.FullName -Recurse -File `
+  -Filter "Invoke-Crm3V42R1CanonicalLocalLab.ps1" |
+  Select-Object -First 1
+
+& $Script.FullName `
+  -CandidatePath $Candidate.FullName `
+  -CurrentAppRoot "C:\Users\abhis\AndroidStudioProjects\crm3_baf_ops" `
+  -EvidenceRoot "$HOME\Downloads" `
+  -RunEmulators `
+  -EmulatorPort 8180
+```
+
+Use a free port if `8180` is occupied.
+
+## Authoritative outcomes
+
+- `PASS_AUTHORITATIVE_BUILD_ONLY`
+- `PASS_AUTHORITATIVE_BUILD_AND_EMULATOR`
+- `PASS_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH_INSTALL`
+
+A diagnostic run, skipped Flutter tests or toolchain mismatch cannot produce an authoritative PASS.
+
+## Fresh-install device proof
+
+After build/emulator success, connect one clean test device on which package `in.co.sail.bsl.crm3.bafops` is absent, then rerun with:
+
+```powershell
+-InstallOnCleanDevice -DeviceId "<adb-device-id>"
+```
+
+The harness refuses a device where the package already exists. It does not uninstall or clear anything. This is intentionally a fresh-install proof, not an old-database upgrade claim.
+
+## Evidence to upload
+
+The run writes:
+
+- `CRM3_V42_R1_CANONICAL_LOCAL_LAB_<timestamp>.zip`
+- its `.sha256.txt` sidecar.
+
+Upload both files. Do not upload the disposable workspace separately unless the run failed and source-level diagnosis is needed.
